00:14:59,860 --> 00:15:02,507
it's the closest thing
to a miracle there is.

245
00:15:03,180 --> 00:15:05,827
What I'm saying is stay
with your girlfriend.

246
00:15:06,980 --> 00:15:08,686
Pass a message on to Grandma.

247
00:15:09,360 --> 00:15:12,677
Tell her that I'm getting married
and leading the Poison Clan.

248
00:15:12,760 --> 00:15:13,642
Just one catch.

249
00:15:13,900 --> 00:15:16,697
No one gets to decide who
my partner is except me.

250
00:15:16,780 --> 00:15:17,610
Got that?

251
00:15:18,180 --> 00:15:20,080
Wait, so are you being serious?

252
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:23,332
You always decide everything on your own.

253
00:15:24,820 --> 00:15:26,644
I'll go ahead and let her know.

254
00:15:26,760 --> 00:15:28,080
See you soon. Bye.

255
00:15:31,520 --> 00:15:32,600
What's the holdup?

256
00:15:32,780 --> 00:15:34,545
I'm going to need a hand here.

257
00:15:34,700 --> 00:15:36,520
Just how do I carry you?

258
00:15:36,780 --> 00:15:39,117
I've never had to pick up a living girl.

259
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:41,160
So where should I grab you?

260
00:15:42,740 --> 00:15:46,858
I don't think you'll have to worry
about that, because I'm not a girl.

261
00:15:47,340 --> 00:15:48,200
Oh, great.

262
00:15:48,460 --> 00:15:50,440
Well, in that case...

263
00:15:51,040 --> 00:15:51,870
Wait.

264
00:15:57,720 --> 00:16:00,380
After a bloodbath, a
shower hits different.

265
00:16:00,840 --> 00:16:03,540
How about it, Kero?
Care to join? No thanks.

266
00:16:04,140 --> 00:16:05,780
What's wrong? Afraid?

267
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:07,420
I said no!

268
00:16:08,300 --> 00:16:11,124
Don't know about you, but
I feel like a new man.

269
00:16:11,980 --> 00:16:12,810
Hilarious.

270
00:16:12,893 --> 00:16:15,417
Bet you're thinking I don't
look like any man you've seen.

271
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:16,794
You're a professional.

272
00:16:17,060 --> 00:16:18,001
Want to confirm?

273
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:20,960
What's your deal?

274
00:16:21,140 --> 00:16:22,937
How come you dress in women's clothing?

275
00:16:23,020 --> 00:16:23,850
Easy.

276
00:16:23,933 --> 00:16:25,577
Because my latest mark was a man.

277
00:16:25,660 --> 00:16:28,484
If I needed to dupe a
woman, I'd dress as a guy.

278
00:16:28,640 --> 00:16:30,877
Plus, it's more fun playing both sides.

279
00:16:30,960 --> 00:16:32,837
That was the best move
you could have made.

280
00:16:32,920 --> 00:16:35,080
Proposing to me, I mean. Hang on!

281
00:16:35,820 --> 00:16:39,702
I can teach you to make anyone
fall for you, regardless of gender.

282
00:16:39,880 --> 00:16:40,998
Hurry up and do it!

283
00:16:41,880 --> 00:16:42,710
Step one.

284
00:16:42,793 --> 00:16:45,545
Here, I registered you
for a matchmaking party.

285
00:16:45,920 --> 00:16:47,357
Complete your profile and boom.

286
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:50,793
Wait, it's after midnight,
which means the event's today.

287
00:16:54,920 --> 00:16:55,877
Profession? No.

288
00:16:55,960 --> 00:16:57,717
Writing the truth is probably a bad idea.

289
00:16:57,800 --> 00:16:59,140
So, self-employed.

290
00:17:00,060 --> 00:17:02,557
There's gonna be way more
men there than women.

291
00:17:02,640 --> 00:17:04,993
I'll captivate the gents with my charms.

292
00:17:05,080 --> 00:17:07,609
That way, there'll be
fewer rivals for you.

293
00:17:08,300 --> 00:17:11,057
Remember, grooming and
fashion only goes so far.

294
00:17:11,140 --> 00:17:13,317
All they do is make a
good first impression.

295
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:16,897
Leveling them up might get you the
nice guy status, but we want more.

296
00:17:16,980 --> 00:17:20,817
No one's going to fall for you unless
we find your charm and let it shine.

297
00:17:20,900 --> 00:17:23,547
Try different approaches
and see what sticks.

298
00:17:25,260 --> 00:17:27,436
Hi there, it's very nice to meet you.

299
00:17:27,900 --> 00:17:30,397
My research indicates first
impressions are everything,

300
00:17:30,480 --> 00:17:33,400
so I've developed the perfect pickup line.

301
00:17:34,520 --> 00:17:35,350
I'm Gero.

302
00:17:36,260 --> 00:17:42,697
I make million a year
my charm is my income

303
00:17:42,780 --> 00:17:44,837
isn't it says right
here money's desirable?

304
00:17:44,920 --> 00:17:47,817
Yeah maybe so but blabbing
about it right out

305
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:49,557
of the gate makes it sound
like you're bragging!

306
00:17:49,640 --> 00:17:54,111
This next girl gaze into her eyes and
smile before you open your dumb mouth.

307
00:18:07,600 --> 00:18:10,797
Maybe I'll research how normal
people smile when I get home.

308
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:12,220
Kero, looky here.

309
00:18:13,340 --> 00:18:17,297
A dating app will give you a chance to
get your bearings when talking to girls.

310
00:18:17,380 --> 00:18:19,637
And good news, I got
you matched right away.

311
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:22,014
You'll have a ton of chances with this.

312
00:18:24,140 --> 00:18:25,100
You good?

313
00:18:25,860 --> 00:18:29,077
A poison master should never eat
anything someone else serves him.

314
00:18:29,160 --> 00:18:31,336
It's the only way to protect himself.

315
00:18:32,060 --> 00:18:35,197
But I doubt anyone's after
my life this second, right?

316
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:37,617
Right I'm sure it will be safe.

317
00:18:37,700 --> 00:18:39,937
See I'm doing totally fine.

318
00:18:40,020 --> 00:18:41,280
I'm doing great.

319
00:18:43,520 --> 00:18:47,257
Okay on to the next girl and

320
00:18:47,340 --> 00:18:51,060
the next one and the next?

321
00:19:03,460 --> 00:19:04,290
Impressive.

322
00:19:04,373 --> 00:19:06,617
Over the course of today,
I've met nearly 30 women,

323
00:19:06,700 --> 00:19:09,777
and somehow I didn't exchange
contact info with even one.

324
00:19:09,860 --> 00:19:13,331
You did your best, so don't go
beating yourself up over it.

325
00:19:14,360 --> 00:19:15,957
Our goal is to find your charm.

326
00:19:16,040 --> 00:19:18,497
But while we're working hard
to figure out what that is,

327
00:19:18,580 --> 00:19:23,168
it would have been kind of nice if at
least one date had gone moderately okay.

328
00:19:23,520 --> 00:19:27,755
Kinosaki, have you entertained the
idea of maybe I don't have any charm?

329
00:19:28,260 --> 00:19:29,090
Don't say that.

330
00:19:29,173 --> 00:19:30,180
I know you do.

331
00:19:30,400 --> 00:19:32,857
It's just hidden, so we
can't see what it is yet.

332
00:19:32,940 --> 00:19:35,528
I promise we'll find
someone who's into you.

333
00:19:36,100 --> 00:19:39,897
It seems bleak, but I promise after
I'm finished polishing you up,

334
00:19:39,980 --> 00:19:43,217
some lucky lady is going to
realize that you're the one.

335
00:19:43,300 --> 00:19:46,771
And after watching you, I found
one thing we can work with.

336
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:47,882
Please tell me.

337
00:19:48,600 --> 00:19:49,960
DIY candy kits.

338
00:19:51,200 --> 00:19:54,357
People with niche hobbies can have
a great time chatting about them.

339
00:19:54,440 --> 00:19:57,337
Also, is it just me or is
this cleaner wicked strong?

340
00:19:57,420 --> 00:19:59,949
It's a mixture I came
up with called Joker.

341
00:20:00,140 --> 00:20:04,437
Using deadly poison to combat stubborn
stains is my favorite way to de-stress.

342
00:20:04,520 --> 00:20:08,777
I can make cleaning agents strong enough
to melt iron when I set my mind to it.

343
00:20:08,860 --> 00:20:11,157
Oh, does this count as
another niche hobby?

344
00:20:11,240 --> 00:20:13,900
Let's just keep that a secret between us.

345
00:20:17,220 --> 00:20:18,500
There you are.

346
00:20:19,280 --> 00:20:20,520
I'm this way.

347
00:20:20,760 --> 00:20:21,857
Guess this is goodnight.

348
00:20:21,940 --> 00:20:22,880
Until tomorrow.

349
00:20:23,400 --> 00:20:24,230
Sure.

350
00:20:24,680 --> 00:20:27,117
Wait, you're putting me
through more torture tomorrow?

351
00:20:27,200 --> 00:20:28,030
So soon?

352
00:20:43,600 --> 00:20:44,480
Hey, Kinosaki.

353
00:20:45,120 --> 00:20:47,657
Want to tell me what you
did to my big brother?

354
00:20:47,740 --> 00:20:48,570
Huh?

355
00:20:48,653 --> 00:20:49,957
Spare me the dumb blonde act.

356
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:53,037
He said he was going to shake
up this lame-ass industry.

357
00:20:53,120 --> 00:20:57,697
Never could shut up about his big plans,
making those old farts beg for mercy.

358
00:20:57,780 --> 00:21:01,257
Now he wants to take over our
parents' dry-cleaning service.

359
00:21:01,340 --> 00:21:04,164
Maybe he just got tired
of life in the big city?

360
00:21:09,800 --> 00:21:11,682
These are white pellets, though.

361
00:21:13,080 --> 00:21:15,577
That's the kind of look
that gets my blood pumping.

362
00:21:15,660 --> 00:21:18,057
You're going to tell me
everything that went down.

363
00:21:18,140 --> 00:21:20,957
And if you beg for your life
like you mean it, who knows?

364
00:21:21,040 --> 00:21:25,077
I might give you a no - I'd rather die
than team up with trash that con civilians.

365
00:21:25,160 --> 00:21:26,220
You're human scum!

366
00:21:28,520 --> 00:21:30,049
You've got some guts, huh?

367
00:21:30,300 --> 00:21:33,065
You take advantage of
folks the same way we do.

368
00:21:33,240 --> 00:21:35,697
I hate criminals with half-assed morality.

369
00:21:35,780 --> 00:21:38,477
If you can't see a crime as a
crime regardless of the target,

370
00:21:38,560 --> 00:21:40,617
you're not cut out for
this line of work, honey.

371
00:21:40,700 --> 00:21:42,977
That pretty face is the
best weapon you've got,

372
00:21:43,060 --> 00:21:45,817
and I'm gonna make sure
you never use it again.

373
00:21:45,900 --> 00:21:48,194
This next shot will be a shotgun blast.

374
00:21:49,880 --> 00:21:50,840
Hey, boss!

375
00:21:51,460 --> 00:21:52,290
There!

376
00:21:55,260 --> 00:21:56,090
It's Gato.

377
00:21:56,560 --> 00:21:58,300
I see him! Floor it!

378
00:22:16,400 --> 00:22:18,100
Oh, my God.

379
00:22:43,240 --> 00:22:46,416
Taking over the dry cleaning
biz doesn't sound so bad.

380
00:22:51,800 --> 00:22:52,920
You dropped this.

381
00:22:54,040 --> 00:22:54,980
My phone.

382
00:22:55,760 --> 00:22:57,900
I wanted to thank you, Kinosaki.

383
00:22:58,240 --> 00:23:00,117
There's no way I could
have met so many women

384
00:23:00,200 --> 00:23:02,097
in one day without your
guidance and support.

385
00:23:02,180 --> 00:23:06,533
A single rejection would have left me
broken up and moping for a lifetime.

386
00:23:07,480 --> 00:23:08,840
I'm hopeless on my own.

387
00:23:09,060 --> 00:23:10,236
You're all I've got.

388
00:23:11,200 --> 00:23:12,997
I didn't get anyone's info either.

389
00:23:13,080 --> 00:23:14,260
We both struck out.

390
00:23:14,440 --> 00:23:15,317
I'm talking here!

391
00:23:15,400 --> 00:23:18,459
Hey, how would you feel
about trading yours with me?

392
00:23:22,140 --> 00:23:24,728
I doubt my friends list
will get any longer.

393
00:23:25,940 --> 00:23:26,777
Don't know why.

394
00:23:26,860 --> 00:23:29,036
Because you're dazzling me right now.

395
00:23:30,980 --> 00:23:32,080
Wait, that's it.

396
00:23:32,220 --> 00:23:33,120
I found it.

397
00:23:33,340 --> 00:23:35,222
I think I discovered your charm.

398
00:23:36,660 --> 00:23:39,013
This is the story of the elite assassin,

399
00:23:39,220 --> 00:23:43,220
Poison Master Gero Hikaru,
and his search for a bride.

400
00:23:46,740 --> 00:23:48,957
Today, you're going on your first dates.

401
00:23:49,040 --> 00:23:49,870
For her so.

402
00:23:50,100 --> 00:23:51,177
What will you say to her?

403
00:23:51,260 --> 00:23:52,357
With the intent to marry?

404
00:23:52,440 --> 00:23:53,322
Don't you dare.

405
00:23:53,440 --> 00:23:55,440
Next time, what is charm anyway?
